WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 1.6 · Strategic Foundations
Positioning and comparative advantage

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Answer one question: why you, rather than someone else, or no one?

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:28.504
Positioning is the specific place your initiative will take in its landscape: the need, the people, your approach and why you are well placed. It answers one question: why you, rather than someone else, or no one?

4
00:00:28.904 --> 00:00:29.504
Three parts of a position

5
00:00:29.504 --> 00:00:40.463
Your focus: The need you focus on, the people you serve and your approach. For example: Paid baking traineeships for young people in one neighbourhood who left school early.

6
00:00:40.463 --> 00:00:52.533
Your advantage: Why you are well placed: trust, skills, lived experience, lower costs or access. For example: One co-founder has ten years of baking; the other, six years working with young people.

7
00:00:52.533 --> 00:01:07.285
Your choices: What you will not do, who you will not prioritise yet and what you refer to others. For example: No café tables for now; young people needing other support go to the youth centre.

8
00:01:07.685 --> 00:01:08.285
Why it matters

9
00:01:08.285 --> 00:01:13.589
1. Saying no protects quality when time and money are limited.

10
00:01:13.589 --> 00:01:19.633
2. Partners can see where you fit and how to work with you.

11
00:01:19.633 --> 00:01:26.307
3. Funders and customers want to know why you, not someone else.

12
00:01:26.707 --> 00:01:27.307
What it guides

13
00:01:27.307 --> 00:01:31.870
1. Your strategic objectives: where to put effort first.

14
00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:36.433
2. Your brand and messages, later in the course.

15
00:01:36.433 --> 00:01:42.737
3. Turning down opportunities that pull you away from your gap.

16
00:01:43.137 --> 00:01:43.737
What to avoid

17
00:01:43.737 --> 00:01:48.670
Claiming “passion” or “innovation” without showing what they produce.

18
00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:52.493
Trying to serve everyone at once.

19
00:01:52.493 --> 00:01:58.426
Presenting advantages you still need to prove as facts.

20
00:01:59.026 --> 00:02:00.826
You write your positioning statement and the choices it implies.

21
00:02:00.826 --> 00:02:04.826
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:02:06.326 --> 00:02:09.426
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
